.venv
/outputs
# The accumulating historical archive (Phase 4) is generated data like
# outputs/, not source -- keeps the append-only file from being committed
# run-by-run.
/data/historical/
# Generated model artifacts and assembled training frames (v1.3 Phase 1) --
# like /data/historical/, not source; regenerable via forecast_training.py.
/data/models/
# Generated experiment caches and reports (v1.3 Phase 3) -- like
# /data/models/, not source; regenerable via forecast_leadtime_calibration.py
# and forecast_experiment.py.
/data/experiment/
# Shadow-prototype prediction logs and the collector's lock file (project
# pivot, 2026-10-05) -- generated per-run, not source.
# `/data/shadow/models/` is DELIBERATELY NOT ignored (2026-10-06): the
# trained .joblib artifacts there must reach the GitHub Actions runner,
# which has no other way to obtain them (no network access to retrain,
# and the cached ABLATION-basis data they're fit from isn't shipped
# either) -- without this carve-out every scheduled run silently falls
# back to raw_forecast, never producing the real ml_wind_corrected
# prediction the collector exists to log. Revisit if the model is
# retrained after the 2026-11-01 freeze point.
/data/shadow/predictions/
/data/shadow/.collect.lock
.env
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.claude